%% aoneahsan-cccs-supabase-realtime — full flow
flowchart TD
    trigger([Live-update work]) --> pick{Which mechanism?}

    pick -->|Postgres Changes| pgc[Row authorisation evaluated<br/>PER SUBSCRIBER PER CHANGE.<br/>Fine for a prototype;<br/>cost grows with subs x writes]
    pick -->|Broadcast from a trigger| bc[You choose the topic and the<br/>PAYLOAD. Authorised once,<br/>at subscribe. Scales]
    pick -->|Presence| pres[Who is here / typing.<br/>Ephemeral by design —<br/>NEVER a source of truth]
    pgc --> bc

    bc --> chan[Private channel]
    chan --> auth[Policy on the messages table:<br/>may THIS user join<br/>THIS topic?]
    auth --> topic[/Topic encodes the scope —<br/>tenant, room, user.<br/>A topic anyone may join<br/>is a public channel/]

    topic --> del{Delivering a DELETE?}
    del -->|expecting the old row| trap[🔴 The old row is not delivered<br/>the way an insert is.<br/>A client cannot filter on a<br/>column it never receives]
    del -->|broadcast a chosen payload| fine[The trigger puts in exactly<br/>what the client needs]
    trap --> fine

    fine --> sub[subscribe -]
    sub --> status{Status callback}
    status -->|SUBSCRIBED| refetch[🔴 REFETCH the backing query —<br/>every time, not just the first]
    status -->|CHANNEL_ERROR / TIMED_OUT| degrade[Degrade visibly.<br/>Do not throw]
    status -->|CLOSED| degrade
    refetch --> gap[/Anything published while<br/>disconnected is GONE.<br/>Realtime is not a durable log/]
    gap --> signal[/So: the event is an INVALIDATION<br/>SIGNAL, the query is what<br/>the UI renders/]

    signal --> base{First delivery?}
    base -->|yes| baseline[Record state, emit NOTHING]
    base -->|no| emit[Emit]
    baseline --> why[/Without it every reload replays<br/>existing rows as fresh events —<br/>a screen of stale alerts about<br/>things already handled/]

    emit --> bounds{Bounded and scoped?}
    bounds -->|unbounded| fetchall[🔴 The fetch-all defect,<br/>held open]
    bounds -->|limited + filtered on the<br/>column the policy reads| good[Provable. And the refetch<br/>uses the same filter]
    bounds -->|structurally small| exempt[Legitimate — carries a<br/>// bounded: reason comment]
    fetchall --> good

    good --> life[Lifecycle]
    exempt --> life
    life --> owner[ONE owner holds the handle.<br/>Tear the previous listener down<br/>BEFORE creating a new one]
    owner --> cleanup[Cleanup removes the channel —<br/>and survives StrictMode's<br/>mount / unmount / remount]

    cleanup --> jwt{Token refreshed?}
    jwt -->|socket keeps the old JWT| stale[🔴 Works for an hour, then stops.<br/>Presents as an intermittent<br/>NETWORK fault, not an auth one]
    jwt -->|setAuth on auth-state change| fresh[Subscriptions keep authorising]
    stale --> fresh
    why --> fresh
    pres --> fresh
    degrade --> fresh
